# Line endings, pinned where getting them wrong breaks something.
#
# Most of this repo is authored on Windows and checked out on Windows, and git's own
# normalisation handles that. These are the exceptions: files that are read by a Unix shell or
# a JVM on a CI runner, where a stray carriage return is not a cosmetic difference.

# The Gradle wrapper is a shell script. With CRLF, /bin/sh fails on the shebang line with a
# message that names a program nobody typed. It is also the entry point for any macOS or Linux
# build, so this is the one file whose endings must not follow the platform.
android/gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Binary, and not to be touched at all.
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary

# The locked seed data and pictures. Base64 so that checkouts behave identically everywhere,
# but there is nothing in a diff of a ciphertext blob that anybody wants to read, and the
# pictures alone are twelve megabytes of it.
*.enc -diff
